{:id :EACL-FORMAL-009
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :manual-review
 :seed-or-trace "public-client/cache-disabled/generated-authority"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :scope-confusion
 :affected-versions ["PR 101 worktree before generated-routing audit"]
 :affected-backends [:datomic :datascript :datahike]
 :root-cause
 "Each adapter bound the configured engine selection inside cache/resolve-current!, but its explicit non-cacheable branch invoked the engine before entering that boundary. Cache-disabled, exact, and otherwise bypassed public requests therefore silently ran legacy traversal even when verified-authoritative or verified-shadow was selected."
 :fix
 "Datomic, Datahike, and DataScript now bind the normalized engine selection around every engine evaluation, independently of completed-answer cache eligibility. The cross-backend state trace counts generated compile/initialize/drive/resume/read calls across explicit cache bypasses."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.formal.state-trace-differential-test/generated-cache-and-cursor-state-traces-across-jvm-adapters"
